{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
'''Group A''' was one of four groups of national teams competing in the second stage of the [[1982 FIFA World Cup]]. The group's three matches were staged at the [[Nou Camp]] in [[Barcelona]]. The group consisted of three teams advancing from the first group stage: Group 1 winners [[Poland national football team|Poland]], Group 3 winners [[Belgium national football team|Belgium]] and Group 6 runners-up the [[Soviet Union national football team|Soviet Union]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/82full.html |title=World Cup 1982 finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref>

Poland topped the group and advanced to the semi-finals, where they were defeated by eventual champions [[Italy national football team|Italy]].

==Qualified teams==
The winners of Group 1 and 3 and the runner-up of Group 6 qualified for Group A of the second round.

